<% content_for(:title, "About") %>

<h2>About</h2>
<p>
  I'm a backend and infrastructure engineer with about a decade of
  experience building production systems — subscription billing engines,
  payment integrations, and the cloud infrastructure that keeps them
  running. Most of that has been in Ruby on Rails, with Go and
  Terraform-driven AWS work taking up a bigger share of the job in recent
  years. I've worked across the whole stack when the problem called for
  it — Vue.js and TypeScript included — but backend and infrastructure is
  where I spend most of my time.
</p>

<h3>Tools</h3>
<p>
  Most of my web development is in Ruby and Rails, backed by PostgreSQL,
  with Go for services where performance matters more — plus JavaScript,
  TypeScript, and Vue.js when the frontend needs attention. On the
  infrastructure side I work with Docker, Kubernetes, and Terraform on AWS,
  tied together with GitHub Actions, Ansible, and some Python for
  scripting. I also write some Swift, mostly for small CLI tools and
  native apps.
</p>
